@INPROCEEDINGS{Wessel2020whatexpect,
    AUTHOR="Mairieli Wessel and Alexander Serebrenik and Igor Wiese and Igor Steinmacher and Marco Aurelio Gerosa",
    TITLE="What to Expect from Code Review Bots on {GitHub}? A Survey with {OSS} Maintainers",
    BOOKTITLE="SBES 2020 - Ideias Inovadoras e Resultados Emergentes",
    ADDRESS="",
    DAYS="21-23",
    MONTH="oct",
    YEAR="2020",
    ABSTRACT="Software bots are widely adopted by Open Source Software (OSS) projects to streamline the code review process. Interfacing between developers and automated services, code review bots report continuous integration failures, code quality checks, and code coverage. However, as with any new technology adoption, bots may impact maintenance tasks in unexpected ways. In this paper, we study how project maintainers experience code review bots. We surveyed 127 maintainers and asked about their expectations and perception of changes incurred by code review bots. Our respondents were primarily motivated by automating tasks and enhancing the feedback to developers.",
    KEYWORDS="Open Source Software; Software maintenance and evolution ",
}

